			<div class="content" id="post-content-4698441">
									

<p>As far as interpretation goes, yes, some of that lies on the reader. But as the author, you need to ensure you're getting your ideas across in a succinct and understandable way. I was confused as to what was really going on for a lot of this.</p>
<p>Classification is not dependent on how dangerous or hostile something is. It is about how difficult it is to contain. If, until it is neutralized, they have no way to truly contain it, it's Keter.</p>
<p>And I'm the same person reading the article the whole time. It doesn't make sense that I'd turn into the administrator at the end. And you'd be logged in with the same credentials the whole time.</p>

